From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:39:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] ci: add path-filtered per-tool CI and ported upstream
 checks

- test-python.yml / test-node.yml: reusable test workflows. Python: each tool's Python versions are read from its own test workflow (tools/<tool>/.github/workflows/test.yaml, the old repository's CI), locked dependencies, explicit Python version in every command; query-tool: lint, format, Cypress component and e2e, as upstream (typecheck and codespell run in the commit hooks).
- api, federation-api, configure-nb, query-tool workflows: run when the tool, the folders it links to (recipes/, examples/) or the shared workflow changes. api deselects its service-dependent integration tests.
- recipes has no CI here yet: its own workflows keep running in the old recipes repository (on the mirror's pull requests and on their schedule) until they are redone.
- query-tool examples: diff against examples/ on PRs (comment workflow), update PR on main.
- link-check.yml: api linkspector with its own config.
- stale, scorecard and handle_external_pr ported from the org templates.
